title: From far away, a file coloured by an extension's grammar shows its bars in the grammar's colours once it has been painted, and Rust keeps the app's own
folders: grammars
extensions: grammar-extension
expect-log: script: bars of src/hello\.quill from the app: 3 blocks, text · text · text$
expect-log: the grammar of quill coloured src/hello\.quill: 21 of its 21 lines tokenized
expect-log: the grammar of quill coloured big/long\.quill: 6000 of its 6000 lines tokenized
expect-log: script: bars of src/hello\.quill from its grammar: 3 blocks, (?!text · text · text)
expect-log: script: bars of big/long\.quill from its grammar: 750 blocks,
expect-log: script: bars of src/main\.rs from the app: 1 blocks,
forbid-log: script: bars of big/long\.quill from the app
forbid-log: WARN.*script

resize 1600 1000
wait 2500
bars src/hello.quill
fit
wait 1200
mark far-before
wait 400
goto src/hello.quill
wait 2500
goto big/long.quill
wait 4000
bars src/hello.quill
bars big/long.quill
bars src/main.rs
fit
wait 1500
mark far-painted
wait 400
goto src/hello.quill
wait 1500
zoom 0.02
wait 1200
mark hello-blocks
wait 400
quit
